## 9. UI Expectations & Behaviour Rules

### Spacing & Layout
- Sidebar items: 40px tall, px-3, gap-1
- Cards: rounded-xl, p-4, subtle shadow (`shadow-sm`)
- Section headings: text-xs uppercase tracking-wider text-tertiary, mb-2
- Content max-width inside Workspace: max-w-3xl, mx-auto (for editor)
- Grid spacing: gap-4 for cards

### Interactive States
- Hover: bg-hover transition-colors duration-150
- Active/Selected: bg-selected + accent left border (2px)
- Focus rings: ring-2 ring-accent/40 ring-offset-2
- Disabled: opacity-50, cursor-not-allowed

### Motion (Framer Motion — keep subtle)
- Sidebar collapse: width transition 200ms ease
- Inspector slide: x-axis, 250ms ease-out
- Modal appear: scale 0.96 → 1.0, opacity 0 → 1, 180ms
- Toast appear: slide-in from right, 200ms
- Page transitions: none (instant, no full-page animation)

### Auto-save UX
- StatusBar shows "Saving…" → "Saved just now" → "Saved 2m ago"
- No save button anywhere in the editor
- If offline: "Changes saved locally"

### Empty States
- Every list/grid must have an EmptyState component
- Always include: Icon (Lucide, 40px, text-tertiary) + Heading + Subtext + Primary CTA
- Examples:
  - No spaces: "Create your first Space" → "Create Space" button
  - No artifacts: "Start capturing knowledge" → "New Artifact" button
  - No search results: "Nothing found" → "Try different keywords"
  - No goals: "Set your first goal" → "Add Goal" button

### Loading States
- Use Skeleton loaders (not spinners) for content areas
- Skeleton cards should match the shape of the actual card
- TopBar search: instant (no loader)
- Artifact Editor: skeleton for content area while loading blocks

### Context Menus (right-click)
Both SpaceCard and ArtifactCard must respond to right-click:
```
SpaceCard context menu:
  Open | Favorite | Pin | Rename | Archive | Delete

ArtifactCard context menu:
  Open | Duplicate | Move to Space | Favorite | Archive | Copy ID | Delete
```

### Notifications (Toast)
- Position: top-right
- Auto-dismiss: 4s for success/info, persist for error
- Types: success (green), warning (amber), error (red), info (blue)
- Keep messages under 60 characters

