## 13. TipTap Block Editor Setup

Configure TipTap with these extensions (minimum for Phase 1):

```typescript
extensions: [
  StarterKit,          // paragraph, heading (h1-h3), bold, italic, strike, code, blockquote, lists
  Underline,
  CodeBlockLowlight,   // with lowlight syntax highlighting
  Image,
  Table, TableRow, TableHeader, TableCell,
  TaskList, TaskItem,  // for checklist
  Placeholder.configure({ placeholder: 'Start writing…' }),
  CharacterCount,
]
```

**Editor visual styling:**
- Font: var(--font-sans), text-base, leading-relaxed
- No editor border or box-shadow — full-width, seamless
- Headings: h1 text-2xl font-semibold, h2 text-xl font-medium, h3 text-lg
- Code blocks: bg-subtle, font-mono, text-sm, rounded-lg, p-4
- Blockquotes: border-l-4 border-accent-light pl-4 italic text-secondary
- Task items: custom checkbox using Tailwind + Lucide Check icon
- On `Cmd/Ctrl + /` → show slash command palette (block type picker)

**Slash Commands (type `/` to trigger):**
```
/heading1  /heading2  /heading3
/paragraph /bullet /numbered /checklist
/code /quote /callout /divider
/image /table
```

---

## 14. Knowledge Graph (React Flow)

- Nodes: one per Artifact in the current Space
- Node size based on relationship count (more connections = slightly larger)
- Node color: matches artifact type color
- Edges: labeled with relationship type
- Controls: zoom in/out, fit view, minimap
- Click a node → opens that Artifact in the editor
- Hover a node → show tooltip with title + type + relationship count
- Default layout: Force-directed (dagre or elk layout)
- Background: dotted grid pattern (React Flow default, subtle)

